# Rotating View with Mouse

Common FPS camera rotation:
```csharp
float mouseX = Input.GetAxis("Mouse X");
float mouseY = Input.GetAxis("Mouse Y");
transform.Rotate(Vector3.up * mouseX * sensitivity);
// For camera pitch (vertical), rotate around local X axis
```

You usually lock the cursor: `Cursor.lockState = CursorLockMode.Locked;` and hide it: `Cursor.visible = false;`.

slides.codeSnippet:
public float sensitivity = 2f;
void Update()
{
    float mouseX = Input.GetAxis("Mouse X") * sensitivity;
    float mouseY = Input.GetAxis("Mouse Y") * sensitivity;
    transform.Rotate(0, mouseX, 0); // yaw
    // For pitch, you'd need a separate child object
}
